# SmartVitals Prototype #

**AI-enabled vital signs wearable for virtual care: clinician dashboard and patient view**

> **Concept only.** This is a feasibility study software prototype. It is not a medical device and not a clinical decision support system. All patient and sensor data is simulated.

## About

SmartVitals is a feasibility study into a next generation wearable device that supports remote patient monitoring for virtual care. This repository contains a **software prototype** of the clinician dashboard and a simplified patient view that show how the data from the wearable device could be monitored and acted on.

It is part of the La Trobe University CSE3CAP capstone.

## Background

Care is modernize and moving out of hospitals and into people's home, through programs like the Victorian Virtual Emergency Department (VVED) and hospital-at-home. Existing wearables device are mostly single use, they sample at low rates and rely on separate gateway hardware.

The SmartVitals concept is a **reusable, rechargeable, cellular-connected wearable** that combines PPG, rPPG, ECG and temperature sensing with on device AI, targeting a sampling rate of 500 samples per second. The wider study covers four major areas:

| Area | Focus |
|---|---|
| Technical | Sensor design and signal-quality benchmarking |
| Clinical | End-to-end workflow map, enrolment to discharge |
| Regulatory | TGA pathway (preliminary Class IIb) and ISO 13485 / ISO 14971 review |
| Commercial | University-led manufacturing compared with existing vendors |

## What this prototype shows

| Route | Screen |
|---|---|
| `/` | Prototype clinician login |
| `/dashboard` | Patient monitoring table |
| `/alerts` | Critical and warning alert triage |
| `/patients/[id]` | Patient detail: vitals, simulated ECG and SpO2 trend charts, wearable device health, deterioration panel and clinical actions |
| `/patient-view` | Simplified patient mobile view, showing role separation |

Clinicians can acknowledge an alert and add a clinical note from the patient detail screen. 

## How it fits the system architecture

| Architecture component | In this repository |
|---|---|
| Wearable patch | Simulated. Device health (battery and signal) is shown from sample values |
| Patient mobile app | Simplified patient view (`/patient-view`) |
| VVED clinical relay | Not implemented |
| Cloud services | Not implemented. Data is hard-coded in `lib/data.ts` |
| Clinician dashboard | Implemented (dashboard, alerts and patient detail screens) |

